In article <29qc53$4n9@nic.lth.se>, tg@loglady.df.lth.se (Tomas Gradin) writes:
> How do I remove a disk pack from an RA60 drive?
> I placed it in the drive by putting it there, turning the handle a few
> turns, and then simply removing the cover. The opposite doesn't work,
> however, so I would appreciate any help in this matter.

  I assume you've got the top cover open and can see the pack. If not, send
mail for detailed instructions on how to break into an RA60 drive 8-)

  You need the pack cover. Gently place the pack cover on top of the pack.
Rotate the handle while wiggling the cover, so that the tab in the cover
will catch one of the dimples in the pack hub. This is usually obvious. Now,
"unscrew" the pack by turning the handle counterclockwise *without* lifting
the handle.

  If you have an older (or broken) drive, the latch that's supposed to keep
the whole pack + cover from rotating may be missing (or broken). In that 
case, you'll have to hold the cover while turning the handle.

