license to do so. So we cannot take advantage of software renderers in
other company products.

Although OpenGL uses X through the GLx extension to the server, you cannot
put this server on any Alpha without 3D hardware, so you can only display
over the network to other systems with 3D hardware.

I have it running on a 3000/400 with a PXG board. It works very well and is
very easy to do things and is reasonably fast. This is so even though the
DEC implementation (AUX library) is crude at this point.

I think all this is correct. If not, will someone out there please correct
me.

If anyone out there knows of a company that will be implementing openGL on
the DEC Alphas without 3D hardware.

John Boccio
