    Once, a long time ago, it was built into VMS (or the
 equivalent was).  If you bought VMS before a certain date (quite
 a few years ago) you could get VAX-11/RSX without paying for the
 license.  All such offers expired quite some time ago.

    There are disassemblers for PDP-11/RSX tasks which work fairly
 well.  You could concieveably turn an image (or better, an object
 file) back into Macro-11 source code if it's a small program.  If
 it's a big program, you'll probably have to re-write it.



