Sorry, in a workstation environment failover is as important as in 'large
shops'. A workstation cluster usually has some common server for disks,
and this is a single point of failure for the entire cluster. We have here
a rather large DECstaton clusetr, and smaller VAXstation cluster. On DEC
I find once per week (average) a nice message 'nfs server not responding,
still trying...' - and it means that for some time I have to do something
else. On VMS cluster one of the boot nodes got a problem and had to be
rebooted a few days ago - and people working at the workstations didn't notice
it. The secret is that we have two boot nodes shadowing each other's disks,
and serving the to all workstations. 
