You are sure that none of the bulbs have failed :-)

>Is the disk not reaching a high enough speed?

The disk must be turning for the drive to become ready, but if it takes too
long, then the drive will fault. The drive becomes ready after the heads have
loaded and the servo locked onto a spinning pack. Almost any failure here will
give a fault.
Power  up the drive with the logic cover removed (hook it onto the back of the
drive), and the read-write box flipped out. Does it ever try to load the heads?
Has the drive ever worked (you don't have the head shipping lock on?).


> 
