The surprising item to me is the big raise in the 300 SBB, although
I suppose it makes sense. If you figure, realistically, the a VRT19
goes for about $2000 and a 1GB SCSI disk is worth about $1000, the
difference between the SBB and Packaged system should be about $3000.
However it had been $12,995 - $7,495 = $5,500 so you were paying $2500
"extra" for the packaged system (and getting NOTHING for it). Now
those figures are more in line, you are only paying $3300 for VRT19 +
RZ26, which is not so unreasonable. (Note also though that the
discounts had been much bigger for packaged .vs. SBB). I guess this is
also why the 400 Packaged system was dropped while the SBB stayed the
same.

