One point ("feature"?) that a lot of people seem to forget about VMS help is
"Hints" topic.  That's the place to look if you have absolutely no clue what
you're looking for (in specific), but you have a general idea of what you want
to do.  Most systems I manage I take the time to extract the Hints topic and
add to it information about layered product and DECUS stuff that have been
added to the system.

Another feature that is often overlooked is that you can specify wildcards at
any time and get everything from that subtopic on down, avoiding having to
navigate a tree structure.

Third, a word about piping...granted, piping is something VMS is lacking that
is very useful.  But it can be emulated fairly easily.  I do it via a command
procedure call PIPE.COM (original, eh?) that I believe I obtained from one
DECUS tape or another, and which I've beefed up a little.  Thus, to find out
information about a specific user or process I do:

   $ PIPE SHO SYS | GREP DOEJ

or, using another command procedure I wrote which gives me a little different
information that SHOW SYSTEM, to find out all users running a particular image,
I do:

   $ PIPE DPROC/USER | GREP OA$MAIN

or even

   $ PIPE DPROC/USER | GREP OA$MAIN | MORE

It's not perfect, but it does what I need done, and more and more people at our
site are discovering the usefullness.  Even the Unix folks are (somewhat!)
impressed.

Dennis Couch


