=        Yes.  Pick up the PD version  of DELIVER, available on the DECUS
=    tapes,  file  servers and ftp sites everywhere :-).  If any  of  the
=    CERN VAXen are  running  PMDF,  DELIVER  is  included  in  the  PMDF
=    distribution.   Another  possibility  is  to  use  MX,  which  is  a
=    replacement for the VMS Mail  interface (mail user agent?).

No, MX is *NOT* a replacement for the VMS Mail interface.  It is an MTA (mail
transport agent).  You still compose and read mail using VMS MAIL.  The only
sense in which MX can be considered a replacement for VMS Mail is that you can
configure it to deal with mail intended to be delivered using the MAIL-11
protocol, thus getting the benefit of store-and-forward for mail intended to be
delivered via DECnet.
