All this whining about lack of pipes in VMS in 90% cases boils down to the lack of
only one thing, namely pipng to MORE. This particular thing can be implemented in
an easier and more consistent way at the level of terminal driver, not DCL. For 
example, a command SET MORE=24  or alike would switch the terminal driver to the mode
where it stops after every 24 lines until you hit a key; SET NOMORE would undo it.
BTW, this feature was built into TSX-Plus. Due to the lack of spare time, I am
challenging you folks to implement it in VMS; if no volunteer comes up, I will
probably do it myself, but not right now (probably in Jan-Feb).

