Unless you are running with a blocksize of one character the 'last unfilled
blocks' do exist.  Suppose you are running a BSD file system with a blocksize
of 8192 and a fragment size of 2048.  How many files of size <2048 can you
fit in a disk compared to files of size 2049?  Knowing that you have x files
totaling n bytes doesn't tell you squat about how much of the disk you are
taking up without have other information available such as the fragment
size (or even the file system type).

Doug

