But it is not a real solution: if being able to migrate old programs
to the latest platform is meant to be a benefit, then I >should< be
able to port my old code to the latest VMS running on today's hardware
and have it work.  My example shows that the differences between VAX C
and DEC C are large enough that >even< if the program compiles without
any errors, it is still >NOT< guaranteed to run properly.  Even a DEC
employee related to the DEC C project has said that there are
significant difference between VAX C and DEC C and that migration isn't
necessarily a straightforward recompilation.

