	>[.macro32.savesets].

I did plan to move to a newer version of GNU Awk when I had the time.
I didn't expect the difference between VAX C and DEC C to be great
enough to cause such problems.  VEST is only a temporary solution, and
not a long term one.

The fact is that even on VMS moving programs between architectures can
be as hairy as Unix at times.
