Yeah, come to think of it, why does man insist on formatting pages as if they
are going to be printed out?  Its a great *option*, but, for normal online
reading, I don't need a page header or footer and I don't need 66 line pages
when my terminal is set at 24!

Man was a simple program designed a long time ago and is in definite need of a
revamp.  Some simple improvements that man(1) could use:

1. It should pay attention to stty(1) settings like rows and columns.
2. It should allow headers/footers to be optional.
3. Most manpages already have subheaders, why not have a VMS HELP-like
   approach where users can choose the subheader they're interested in.
4. More flexibility in where manpages are stored and the format that they are
   stored in.

I'm sure more could be thought of...

