The issue is not strictly a VAX-to-Alpha migration issue.
It is a VAX C to DEC C migration issue, which will eventually be
an issue for folks who stay with VAX processors - ie., DEC C should
replace VAX C, so everyone who wrote programs in VAX C, and relied on
it's relative "laxness" in adhering to standards, will have problems.

