asvirsky@lynx.dac.northeastern.edu writes:

>	I need some help with my DF03 modem.  What are the functions of
>the first 4 pushbuttons?  They are in order: ANL  ST  RDL  DTL.
>I understand the purposes of HS and DATA/TALK.
>	Please don't ask me why I use such old equipment.  :)  Just a
>hobby I guess.  Its hooked up to my VT131.  :)

>	Thanks!
>	Alex

>-- 
>	Alex Svirsky			asvirsky@lynx.neu.edu

ANL -- When in analog loopback
ST  -- When in self test
RDL -- When in the remote station connected to the modem is placed
	in digital loopback (high speed only)
DTL -- When in the local modem is conditioned for digital loop
	testing (from a remote modem)
HS  -- When in 1200 baud / when out 0--300 baud

Manual orginate ANL, ST, RDL & DTL out.  HS as desired. DATA/TALK in
When answer tone is heard DATA/TALK out

Manual answer DATA/TALK in, all other buttons out.  Answer ringing
phone, when asked for data connection, DATA/TALK out.

Auto Answer All buttons out

/s/ Jim WIlliams
[Former DEC employee and former RT-11 architect]



