> ETHERNET bandwidth).  

If you're going to criticize something on technical points, at least do so from
a sound technical footing. 

First off the traffic you appear to be worried about is VAXcluster (SCS)
traffic, which is not, repeat not, DECnet.  Yes, both DECnet and SCS have
"keepalive" timers.  However the "chatter" is on the order of a message per
node per one to ten seconds.  And, they don't bother doing this if there is
real traffic.  If ten nodes managed to "clog up" your Ethernet this way,
your either had a very strange Ethernet (1 kilobit/second, maybe?) or else
someone must have gone in and shortened the timers (and patched the code to
allow them to be set to well below the minimums that are normally enforced). 

