> file systems) they couldn't, since file sharing wasn't available... :-(

That's strange, it works for everyone else.  

> I used to love when the VMS cluster would become two clusters
> when quorum was lost.  Really funny!

Once again -- the cluster was obviously misconfigured.  Some node or combo
of nodes had too many votes, or quorum was too low, or possibly both.  That's
what quorum is *for*.  

There are valid criticisms to be made of VMS.  These aren't among them. If I
felt a need to put up straw men to carp about Unix I could easily cite some
examples of terrible behavior in badly misconfigured systems... but I'm not
sure what it would prove. 

