>We can't get sc from the specint92 benchmarks to work correctly
>on the alpha. It compiles OK but doesn't run correctly. 
>Has anyone out there gotten it to work? Because there isn't an
>alpha wrapper (M.alpha) we're not sure how the makefile needs to
>be modified.

sc is a bastard to get right, because its output depends upon the
terminal type and size.  This may work just fine in official SPEC
benchmarking, given that none of the benchmarks require anything more
exciting than a 24x80 terminal to run on (guess what sc assumes), but
tends to cause problems if you are running within a window system.

Be sure that the following little bits appear in your Makefile and
rscript.

From the makefile
=======================
TERM    = vt220
LINES   = 24
COLUMNS = 80
=======================

From the shell script
=======================
#!/bin/sh
...
	TERM=${TERM} LINES=${LINES} COLUMNS=${COLUMNS} \
	./072.sc $INITFILE < $ii >> $output
...
=======================

