cornec@stna.dgac.fr (Cornec ESLOG p8023 BD17) writes:

>Is there any document, available from anonymous ftp 
>giving me informations on porting software from a 32bit machine
>(ADA Verdix compiler) to AXP 64bit machine (DEC ADA complier)

>I know such a document exists for the C language. Is there a corresponding
>one for ADA ?

You don't need a specific document for Ada.  The issues are exactly the same
for C and Ada:  data types change, cache interference, data alignment, byte
granularity, register and address sizes change, instructions can be
re-ordered, memory page size is not fixed at 512.  If you have ported to
any risc platform before, you have seen these issues.  If you have written
files using sequential_io or direct_io, you'll have to figure out how to
rewrite them for 64bit. 

The only additional changes you will face are that you'll have a different
Ada runtime and different memory management algorithms.
