Just to clear up some confusion and, I hope, not create any more:

DIA is the replacement for DSIN, which allows electronic access to the
CSC (both problem submission and information database access) from any
VT-compatible terminal, including emulators.  DSIN has much the same
functionality as DSNlink, but does not require software installed on
the customer's system.  It is meant as a partner to DSNlink such that
any information that DSNlink has access to is also available from
DSIN.

DIA is a worldwide tool that will add file/patch copy functionality to
the current DSIN functions.  All current DSIN users will migrate to
DIA when it is available in the next calendar year.

There are no absolutely no plans to replace or eliminate DSNlink, and
in fact new versions for the OpenVMS, Ultrix, and OSF/1 systems are
in development now.

Please post any further questions here that I can help with.

Dan Barrett
US DSNlink/DIA Program Manager
