VAXen.  All the stuff one expects with TCP/IP works just great between
VMS and UNIX (SunOS, IRIX, HPUX, OSF/1, etc.), including rcp, telnet, ftp,
finger, email, NFS file cross-mounting, etc.   And the TGV-ware co-exists
on the same wire with DECnet.

