It's actually pretty simple why we won't use Alpha.  There is a couple
of million dollars worth of Vax equipment in the software development
lab, and nobody is willing to take the chance that anything developed
and compiled on Vax machines will run on Alpha machines.  Also, the
inhouse knowledge of the Vax architecture is considerable, while
nobody knows the Alpha.  Finally, it is not yet clear that all
required COTS software is available for the Alpha.  The Vax offers
acceptable performance with little risk.

Barry Smith




