Just in  case anyone else is running the OSF/1 - Flashdat 2d+ combination,
I thought I'd post the solution I've found.

If you apply the DEC Archive python patch, and set up your cam_data.c entry
as follows all seems to work fine.


/* ARCHIVE Python - DAT drive */
{"ARCHIVE Python", 14, DEV_TLZ04,
 (ALL_DTYPE_SEQUENTIAL << DTYPE_SHFT) | SZ_RDAT_CLASS,
  (struct pt_info *)ccmn_null_sizes, SZ_NO_BLK, 0x10000, 
  &tlz04_dens, NO_MODE_TAB, SZ_NO_FLAGS,
  NO_OPT_CMDS, SZ_READY_DEF, SZ_NO_QUE, DD_REQSNS_VAL | DD_INQ_VAL,
  24, 36
},



Apparently the digidat compressor board in the unit can only handle a maximun
transfer size of 64K and the tlz04 entry I cloned it from has (DEC_MAX_REC - 1)
which I think translates to 128K.


Richard
