I have my 500x turned into a server. There are 2 things you have to do:

1) move the Alternate console switch (S3?) to the left, towards the MMJ 
   printer port loated in the back of the 500X box.

2) in console mode (>>) type SET SERVER ON. This is important. It tells 
   the system to pass startup diagnostics, and continue with booting.
   If this is not set, diagnostics will detect the absence of monitor,
   keyboard, and the system will not autoboot. You will have to boot it
   manually.

Of course, you will have to install the proper OPENVMS-ALPHA-USER license
with enough units to allow multiuser sessions. If you have CSLG you then
have the appropriate PAK.


